<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Voice Typer — macOS hardened-runtime entitlements
  (ADR-0020 §13.2 + docs/migration/signing-guide.md "Hardened runtime entitlements")

  Consumed by the codesign invocation with the entitlements flag pointing
  at this file, for:
    - the Nuitka sidecar binaries (python-sidecar-x86_64-apple-darwin,
      python-sidecar-aarch64-apple-darwin)
    - the prewarm binaries (prewarm-x86_64-apple-darwin,
      prewarm-aarch64-apple-darwin)
    - the .app bundle (codesign deep-sign invocation with entitlements flag)

  BUILD-N02: the previous plist shipped only 3 entitlements and silently
  dropped two that are required for the universal .app to function on
  macOS 14+ under the hardened runtime. Added:
    - allow-unsigned-executable-memory — Nuitka onefile loaders allocate
      RWX pages when unpacking the embedded payload; without this
      entitlement macOS 14 kills the process with EXC_BAD_ACCESS at
      startup, breaking the sidecar + prewarm binaries (which Nuitka
      froze with --onefile).
    - automation.apple-events — the volume_ducker + clipboard_snapshot
      modules use AppleScript via NSAppleEventDescriptor to drive
      System Events.app (volume ramp, foreground app detection). Without
      this entitlement, every AppleScript invocation fails silently with
      `errAEEventNotPermitted` (-1743) and the duck/clipboard features
      degrade to no-ops.

  The pre-existing three entitlements remain (see ADR-0020 §13.2 for
  justification):
    - allow-jit                      CTranslate2 may use JIT.
    - disable-library-validation     Nuitka onefile extracts unsigned dylibs at runtime.
    - device.audio-input             Mic access (sounddevice).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
